  "body": "Consider the following scenario:\r\n\r\nTwo user, Tom and Jerry are located in US, but they have matrix accounts on the server locate in France.\r\n\r\nBoth Tom's and Jerry's device are connected to the internet via their own home WiFi router (under NAT). So direct connection is not possible.\r\n\r\nFor the current settings, if Tom want to make a 1:1 video call with Jerry. He need to relay his data through the TURN server in France. This will not only make it inefficient but also make the connection unstable.\r\n\r\nIt would be nice to firstly communicate with the STUN server in France (this is one-time interaction), and then the STUN server will provide a public TURN server located in US (between Tom and Jerry in network topology). And let Tom and Jerry relay their connection via this US TURN server.\r\n\r\n\r\nThis design can utilize decentralized resource more efficient. \r\n",
